      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-326103",
      ":question/problem": "A camera shop buys a prime lens at a set wholesale cost. The shop marks up the lens by $30%$ to set the retail price. During a promotion, the lens is sold at a discount equal to $20%$ of the retail price. If the discounted price of the lens is $$78.00$, what is the wholesale cost of the lens?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
